0..78 Comment "//! `cancelled-receiver` models a peer that waits after a handler abandons its"
79..96 Comment "//! continuation."
97..100 Comment "//!"
101..176 Comment "//! It proves that a waiting peer observes cancellation at its next action."
177..227 Comment "//! An abandoned end also cancels each queued end."
228..231 Comment "//!"
232..282 Comment "//! Each program exits from its root continuation."
283..326 Comment "//! The handler abandons that continuation."
327..346 Comment "//! It returns `7`."
347..350 Comment "//!"
351..392 Comment "//! - see: #3305 — the cancellation hop"
393..475 Comment "//! - cites: [Fowler-2019-exceptional_asynchronous_session_types] — cancellation"
476..546 Comment "//!   reaching the peer and every end left in a cancelled end\'s buffer"
547..550 Comment "//!"
551..717 Comment "//! [Fowler-2019-exceptional_asynchronous_session_types]: https://doi.org/10.1145/3290341 \"Fowler, Lindley, Morris and Decova, Exceptional Asynchronous Session Types\""
719..772 Comment "// The import provides the early-exit host interface."
